        <body>
            <div xml:id="d68">

                <pb facs="0486" n="472" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg472"/>

                <head>[64]<hi rendition="#italic">*Mr. McCulloch, collector, to Mr. Zamorano Spanish
                        consul.</hi></head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Custom-House,
                            Baltimore</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Collector’s
                        Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1817-04-14"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">April</hi> 14, 1817</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: If you can name the vessel and specify any
                    circumstance to warrant the proceeding, immediate attention will be paid to the
                    object by pursuing her course as far as possible.</p>
                <p>Allow me to say that if your note just received respects the ship Idas, she was
                    searched by me in consequence of certain suspicions on Saturday evening, and was
                    found without arms, ammunition, or any warlike equipment, and cleared in ballast
                    coastwise.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>J. H. McCULLOCH.</item>
                            <item>Don <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joaquin Zamorano</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Consul of Spain.</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
